WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.461 --> 00:00:11.116
Tom Lindqvist: Hey Michelle, hey Brandon. Thanks for making time this afternoon. I know things have been busy on your side.

2
00:00:12.449 --> 00:00:20.621
Michelle Tran: Hi Tom. Yeah, it's been a week. Brandon's joining because he's been hearing about this from his supervisors too.

3
00:00:21.361 --> 00:00:25.565
Brandon Hughes: Morning, Tom. Or afternoon for you. Let's just get into it.

4
00:00:25.975 --> 00:00:35.685
Tom Lindqvist: Of course. So I have the two escalations from earlier this quarter in my notes. Want to start with what's happening now, or walk me through the history first?

5
00:00:37.016 --> 00:00:48.816
Michelle Tran: Let's do now. The issue is when Genesys transfers a call between queues or from one agent to another, the PreSense screen pop comes up blank for whoever receives it.

6
00:00:49.486 --> 00:00:56.920
Tom Lindqvist: Blank meaning no digital journey data at all, or blank meaning the fields are there but empty?

7
00:00:57.158 --> 00:01:03.970
Michelle Tran: Completely blank. White panel. The agent sees the caller's number and that's it. No pages viewed, no ad source, nothing.

8
00:01:04.324 --> 00:01:08.083
Brandon Hughes: And this isn't every transfer. Michelle, what's the rough rate?

9
00:01:08.617 --> 00:01:19.514
Michelle Tran: We tracked it for two weeks. About one in five transfers. So if a rep takes forty transferred calls a day, eight of them are flying blind.

10
00:01:19.862 --> 00:01:24.853
Tom Lindqvist: Okay. And the first agent, the one who originally answered, they see the pop fine?

11
00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:36.026
Michelle Tran: First agent is fine. It's only after the transfer fires. That's what makes it so frustrating, because the receiving agent is usually the one who needs the context most.

12
00:01:37.162 --> 00:01:40.483
Tom Lindqvist: Got it. When did you first notice it?

13
00:01:41.209 --> 00:01:53.949
Michelle Tran: Middle of July. We raised it with support, they asked for examples, we sent a batch. Then it went quiet for a few weeks and it came back in August, so we raised it again.

14
00:01:54.883 --> 00:02:04.158
Brandon Hughes: And that's why I'm on the call. My supervisors are escalating it internally. They're the ones hearing it from the floor every day.

15
00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:11.400
Tom Lindqvist: That's fair. Can you tell me which queues are involved? Is it specific ones or all of them?

16
00:02:11.657 --> 00:02:20.668
Michelle Tran: Sales primarily. New activations and upgrades. We did see it once in retention but that was a single call, so I don't want to overstate it.

17
00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:31.022
Tom Lindqvist: Understood. And the transfer, is it always agent to agent, or does it also happen when the IVR routes to a queue?

18
00:02:32.179 --> 00:02:38.313
Michelle Tran: Agent to agent mostly. The queue transfers are less common but I've seen a couple.

19
00:02:38.951 --> 00:02:51.443
Tom Lindqvist: Okay. What I'd like to do is get a few call IDs where the receiving agent saw the blank pop, plus the timestamps and the Genesys transfer events if you can pull them.

20
00:02:51.443 --> 00:02:55.985
Tom Lindqvist: That'll let my team line up the PreSense delivery against the transfer.

21
00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:58.639
Brandon Hughes: How many do you need?

22
00:02:59.472 --> 00:03:06.884
Tom Lindqvist: Ten would be plenty. If you can get me ten from different days, that's better than fifty from one afternoon.

23
00:03:08.172 --> 00:03:15.368
Michelle Tran: I can get you ten by Thursday. I'll have my lead pull them from the Genesys reporting side.

24
00:03:15.848 --> 00:03:23.760
Tom Lindqvist: Perfect. And I'll open a case with our engineering team today and reference the two earlier tickets so they see the pattern.

25
00:03:24.518 --> 00:03:34.272
Brandon Hughes: Appreciate that. One thing I want to flag, Tom. We're not asking for a fix on this call. We just need to know it's being looked at seriously.

26
00:03:34.641 --> 00:03:45.339
Tom Lindqvist: I hear that. I can't give you a date today, but I can commit to a status update by end of next week, even if the update is just where it sits.

27
00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:51.392
Michelle Tran: That would help. The silence in August was worse than the bug, honestly.

28
00:03:52.062 --> 00:03:57.947
Tom Lindqvist: Noted. I'll own the updates. Now, separate topic, how are call volumes looking this month?

29
00:03:58.587 --> 00:04:08.112
Michelle Tran: Up. We're averaging around 61,000 calls a month across all campaigns, which is about nine percent over August. Back to school promo is doing a lot of that.

30
00:04:09.086 --> 00:04:12.418
Tom Lindqvist: Nice. Any change on the Google Ads side?

31
00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:18.816
Michelle Tran: No, that's been steady. Offline conversions are flowing. Adobe Analytics is fine too.

32
00:04:19.704 --> 00:04:23.396
Tom Lindqvist: Good. And how's the AI Voice Agent handling the after-hours queue?

33
00:04:23.727 --> 00:04:27.955
Michelle Tran: It's fine. Same as last quarter. No complaints from the team.

34
00:04:28.381 --> 00:04:36.485
Brandon Hughes: We did add six reps to the sales floor in September, so the transfer volume is only going up from here.

35
00:04:37.059 --> 00:04:43.529
Tom Lindqvist: That's useful context. More transfers means more chances for this to show up, so the timing matters.

36
00:04:44.468 --> 00:04:50.185
Michelle Tran: Exactly. And we're heading into Q4 hiring, so it's not going to slow down.

37
00:04:51.180 --> 00:05:02.436
Tom Lindqvist: Okay. Let me recap what I'm taking away. Ten call examples by Thursday, I open the case today, and you get a status from me by end of next week.

38
00:05:02.821 --> 00:05:03.621
Michelle Tran: That works.

39
00:05:04.725 --> 00:05:07.455
Brandon Hughes: Same. Thanks for getting on this, Tom.

40
00:05:08.154 --> 00:05:15.774
Tom Lindqvist: Thanks both. Michelle, send those IDs straight to me and I'll confirm when the case is in. Talk soon.

41
00:05:16.607 --> 00:05:17.775
Michelle Tran: Will do. Bye.

42
00:05:19.195 --> 00:05:19.995
Brandon Hughes: Take care.
